# SQL append-only invariant (epic #522, ADR-013): two sanctioned exceptions only.
# Format: <repo-relative path>  # rationale. Entries must live under an `archive/` directory,
# may only contain a single sanctioned mutating statement (the retention-purge DELETE or the
# archive anonymization UPDATE), and must match a real violation (stale entries fail CI).
#
# Retention purge (ADR-010 / ADR-012). Contract: (1) SELECT from the work DB and copy to the archive DB,
# (2) archive-presence-verify (arhiiv count_present: 100% of the pairs present), (3) this DELETE, called by
# the Ruuter cron only after step 2, deleting only primary keys and only whole entity histories.
DSL/Resql/ljvis/POST/archive/purge_confirmed.sql  # retention purge: verified-archive-then-delete, entity histories whole, by id only

